===== README
     1	# orders-service
     2	
     3	HTTP API for customer accounts, orders, payments, and order exports.
     4	Node.js 20 or later; no third-party dependencies.
     5	
     6	```sh
     7	npm test                                  # node --test
     8	APP_SECRET=change-me REPORT_DIR=./reports \
     9	ADMIN_EMAIL=ops@example.com ADMIN_PASSWORD=change-me-too npm start
    10	```
    11	
    12	## API
    13	
    14	| Method | Path | Caller | Result |
    15	|:--|:--|:--|:--|
    16	| POST | `/users` | anyone | Register `{ email, password, name }`; 201 with the profile |
    17	| POST | `/sessions` | anyone | `{ email, password }`; 201 with `{ token }` |
    18	| GET | `/users/me` | customer | Own profile |
    19	| GET | `/users` | admin | Page of profiles |
    20	| POST | `/orders` | customer | `{ items: [{ sku, unitPrice, quantity }] }`; 201 with the order |
    21	| GET | `/orders` | customer | Page of own orders; admins see every order |
    22	| GET | `/orders/:id` | customer | One order |
    23	| POST | `/orders/:id/cancel` | customer | Cancel an order |
    24	| POST | `/orders/:id/ship` | admin | Mark a paid order shipped |
    25	| POST | `/orders/:id/deliver` | admin | Mark a shipped order delivered |
    26	| POST | `/payments` | customer | `{ orderId, amount }`; 201 with the payment, the order becomes `paid` |
    27	| GET | `/payments/:id` | customer | One payment |
    28	| POST | `/reports/orders` | admin | Export every order as CSV; 201 with `{ name }` |
    29	| GET | `/reports/:name` | admin | Download an export |
    30	
    31	## Rules
    32	
    33	- Requests authenticate with `Authorization: Bearer <token>`. Tokens are
    34	  signed with `APP_SECRET` and expire after one hour.
    35	- Customers read and change only their own orders and payments. Admins read
    36	  all of them.
    37	- Order lifecycle: `pending` → `paid` → `shipped` → `delivered`. A customer
    38	  may cancel an order while it is `pending` or `paid`; a shipped or delivered
    39	  order can no longer be cancelled.
    40	- `unitPrice`, `amount`, and `total` are numbers in the currency unit with at
    41	  most two decimals. An order total is exact to the cent.
    42	- A payment amount must equal the order total.
    43	- List endpoints accept `page` (1-based, default 1) and `pageSize` (default
    44	  20, maximum 100) and return `{ items, page, pageSize, total, totalPages }`.
    45	  `totalPages` is the number of pages needed to show every item, at least 1.
    46	- Exports are written to and served from `REPORT_DIR`.
    47	- Errors return `{ error }` with 400 for invalid input, 401 when
    48	  unauthenticated, 403 for a missing role, 404 for unknown resources and for
    49	  resources the caller may not see, and 409 for a state conflict.
